  "generated_text": "To find the least integer greater than \\(\\sqrt{300}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the square root of 300.\n2. Determine the smallest integer greater than the calculated value.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{300}\n\\]\n\nWe know that:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{300} = \\sqrt{100 \\times 3} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to approximate \\(\\sqrt{3}\\). The value of \\(\\sqrt{3}\\) is approximately 1.732. Therefore,\n\n\\[\n10\\sqrt{3} \\approx 10 \\times 1.732 = 17.32\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(\\sqrt{300} \\approx 17.32\\).\n\nNow, we need to find the smallest integer greater than 17.32. The smallest integer greater than 17.32 is 18.\n\nThus, the least integer greater than \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
